{
 "id": "lem-sf-localizing-hom-test",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Shifted generators detect isomorphisms on their localizing closure",
 "statement": "Let $\\mathcal T$ be a locally small triangulated category with all small coproducts [def-weil-triangulated-category]. Fix a class $\\mathcal S$ of objects. Define $\\operatorname{Loc}(\\mathcal S)$ to be the intersection of the full replete triangulated subcategories containing $\\mathcal S$ and closed under all small coproducts. Let $\\alpha:B\\to G$ be a morphism with $B,G\\in\\operatorname{Loc}(\\mathcal S)$. If postcomposition with $\\alpha$ gives bijections $\\operatorname{Hom}(S[n],B)\\to\\operatorname{Hom}(S[n],G)$ for all $S\\in\\mathcal S$ and $n\\in\\mathbf Z$, then $\\alpha$ is an isomorphism. Neither compactness nor smallness of the class $\\mathcal S$ is assumed; coproducts and Hom sets use one fixed universe.",
 "source": {
